  "changed_since_previous": "No functional changes to the implementation; commit structure and tests document callback destruction behavior and provide atomic shared pointer fallback support.",
  "card": "Modifies btcsignals to eagerly destroy callback function objects when disconnected, restoring boost::signals2 behavior. Currently, callbacks remain alive until the entire signal is destroyed or a subsequent connect call triggers garbage collection. This causes a shutdown hang in multiprocess Bitcoin (#10102) where callbacks hold IPC event loop references that prevent the node process from exiting. It also adds a compatibility fallback for platforms lacking C++20 atomic shared pointer support.",
